      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etoile%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the French word for “star.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/etoile-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Steamboats from Beaumont docked at Brown’s Ferry on the Angelina River just outside Etoile until 1881.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/etoile-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1876 Reverend James Sims built a church at Macedonia Springs, sparking the development of a nearby town called Macedonia.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/etoile-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "By 1897 Etoile hosted the Fisher and Crown General Store, a local hub for residents and travelers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/etoile-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Between the late 1950s and 1965 the Sam Rayburn Dam and Reservoir were constructed nearby, turning the area into a retirement community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
